From: Ubuntu Desktop snaps packaging <desktop-snaps@lists.ubuntu.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: Skip the Calligra Launcher

The launcher/ directory builds a Kirigami/QML start centre for the whole
suite. This snap ships the Words, Sheets and Stage desktop entries directly
and does not stage Qt Quick, Kirigami or Kirigami Addons, so building the
QML module would only produce an unused binary and require extra build
dependencies. Upstream guards the equivalent extras/calligra start centre
with APP_CALLIGRA, but launcher/ is added unconditionally.

Forwarded: not-needed
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -988,7 +988,11 @@
 add_subdirectory(extras)
 add_subdirectory(filters)
 add_subdirectory(data)
-add_subdirectory(launcher)
+# The snap ships the three application entries directly; the launcher is a
+# Kirigami/QML start centre that would require Qt Quick, Kirigami and
+# Kirigami Addons at build and run time. Keep it out of this build.
+#
+#add_subdirectory(launcher)
 
 feature_summary(WHAT ALL INCLUDE_QUIET_PACKAGES FATAL_ON_MISSING_REQUIRED_PACKAGES)
 
